      "writtenOn": "2021-06-29T14:05:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. No, there is no further encryption. This does mean that the plaintext tags in the keyblob are exposed but that amount of exposure didn\u0027t seem problematic for the first iteration. But if it is, we\u0027d have to define a new keyblob format so KM encrypts the whole keyblob (maybe just an extra later of encryption to keep it easy).\n\n2. The would be exported to the host where they can survive a VM reboot, but will be invalidated by a VM update. This is a known and accepted situation for the first iteration.",
      "parentUuid": "d67bc84f_5e39be5b",
